// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 19-concurrency
// facility: rule.conc.spawn [Spawn] (its other arguments are typed as a call of the function); D-0149 (a text literal where a `String` is declared is that `String`); conf.spawn-text-literal-string-argument
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
// expect-stdout-hex: 736c6f7720310a666173742034300a34310a
//
// `spawn(mirror, "fast", 40)` with `mirror` taking `String name`: the
// literal is a `String` there, as in the call `mirror("slow", 1)`.
// (Before the session findings of 2026-11-06 the spawn was rejected,
// `str` against `String`, by a message that itself cited D-0149.)

import std;

fn mirror(String name, u64 n) : u64
{
    printf("%v %v\n", &name, n);
    n + 1
}

fn main()
{
    mirror("slow", 1);
    handle<u64> h = spawn(mirror, "fast", 40);
    printf("%v\n", join(h));
}
